membr:Project_Senger_2610301632_F2610301632 a rsrch:Finding ;
    RDFS:label "(provisional) In American English, the frequency of some of the so-called “GenX so” constructions seem to be declining continuously (Stange 2023). The findings of the project are expected to show how the linguistic behaviour of an individual speaker develops over time in relation to this observed community-level change, and to provide more detailed insights into patterns of age-grading, lifespan change, and retrograde change in the linguistic individual." ;
    rsrch:basedOn cx:engUsSpo_XissoNP .

membr:Senger foaf:currentProject membr:Project_Senger_2610301632 .

references:39b87c34-6766-4f64-9f87-7c249430e507 evid:biblio "Gaston, Phoebe. 2011. Drama SO. Yale Grammatical Diversity Project: English in North America. (Available online at http://ygdp.yale.edu/phenomena/drama-so. Accessed on 2026-10-30). Updated by Tom McCoy (2015) and Katie Martin (2018)." .

references:6f78a661-06f2-4b44-89ce-c5f4bccdabba evid:biblio "Stange, Ulrike. 2020. “Holding Grudges Is So Last Century”: The Use of GenX So as a Modifier of Noun Phrases. Journal of English Linguistics 48(2), 107–136." .

references:bac2aff4-3cd4-4198-8f28-0ce2a5c8eff1 evid:biblio "Gonzálvez-García, Francisco. 2014. “That’s so a construction!” Some reflections on innovative uses of “so” in Present-day English. In María De Los Ángeles Gómez González, Francisco José Ruiz De Mendoza Ibáñez, Francisco Gonzálvez-García & Angela Downing (eds.), Theory and Practice in Functional-Cognitive Space (Studies in Functional and Structural Linguistics), vol. 68, 271–294. Amsterdam: John Benjamins Publishing Company." .

membr:Project_Senger_2610301632 a rsrch:Project ;
    rsrch:hasFindings membr:Project_Senger_2610301632_F2610301632 ;
    rsrch:projectName "How does the linguistic behaviour of an individual speaker develop over time and how do such individual trajectories relate to community-level patterns of variation and change?" .

